{"reference":"Ezra 2","book":"Ezra","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the List","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Ezra 2 is more than a census. Its family groups, priestly eligibility checks, servants, singers, animals, totals, and voluntary gifts together present the returning community as continuous with Israel’s past and organized for life in its cities and worship. The chapter’s total should not be treated as a precise modern census without qualification: the parallel list in Nehemiah 7 differs in places, and ancient counting practices remain uncertain.","verse_refs":["Ezra 2:1-70"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezra_002_9aa4b027203bad37f8fcb1c2"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}